0..57 Comment "/// This source states parametric bridges between values."
58..61 Comment "///"
62..120 Comment "/// A bridge relates endpoints but does not identify them."
121..173 Comment "/// It has no reflexivity, transport, or eliminator."
174..236 Comment "/// At the universe, a bridge is a relation between two types."
237..295 Comment "/// At a type former, it lifts the relations of its parts."
296..299 Comment "///"
300..365 Comment "/// The bridge fold reads a fibre from its carrier and endpoints."
366..435 Comment "/// The checker uses that fibre to validate each bridge introduction."
436..513 Comment "/// The fold reads a list cell by cell, a base type or a sum by its identity,"
514..556 Comment "/// and a function code by extensionality."
557..560 Comment "///"
561..613 Comment "/// - see: corpus/pathological/identity/bridge.gandr"
614..651 Comment "/// - see: #3519 — bridge fold laws"
